---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { LANGUAGE_VERSION, REPO_URL, SOURCE_PUBLIC, VERSION } from '../lib/site.mjs';
---

<Base
  title="About KerfScript"
  description="KerfScript is a programming language for laser cutting, made by MyLaserTools. Find the source, licence and support contact."
>
  <article class="prose narrow">
    <h1>About KerfScript</h1>
    <p>
      KerfScript is a programming language for laser cutting. It lets you describe a design in code,
      adjust its dimensions and export SVG or DXF files. Layers, kerf compensation and joinery are
      built into the language.
    </p>

    <h2>Who makes it</h2>
    <p>
      KerfScript is designed and maintained by <a href="https://mylasertools.com">MyLaserTools</a>, a
      collection of design tools for laser cutting and 3D printing. You can use KerfScript in the
      browser, in MyLaserTools or through the <code>kerf</code> command.
    </p>

    <h2>Current version</h2>
    <p>
      KerfScript {VERSION} implements language version {LANGUAGE_VERSION}. See the
      <a href="/docs/versions/">release policy</a> for compatibility between versions and the
      <a href="/docs/compatibility/">laser software guide</a> for tested file imports.
    </p>

    <h2>Source and licence</h2>
    <p>
      KerfScript is available under the GNU AGPL 3.0, with a separate commercial licence for software
      integrations. You can choose your own licence for the designs and files you create.
      <a href="/licence/">Licence details</a>.
    </p>
    {
      SOURCE_PUBLIC ? (
        <p>
          The source, issue tracker and releases are on <a href={REPO_URL}>GitHub</a>. Install it with
          <code>npm install @mylasertools/kerfscript</code>.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          The source and npm package will be available with the public release. You can try the current
          version in the playground.
        </p>
      )
    }

    <h2>Reporting a problem</h2>
    <p>
      Send your <code>.kerf</code> file and a description of the problem to <a href="mailto:julia@mylasertools.com"
        >julia@mylasertools.com</a
      >{SOURCE_PUBLIC && <>, or open an issue on <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues`}>GitHub</a></>}. Include the name and version of your laser software if the issue involves an exported file.
      Report security issues by email.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
